[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: What a colour means, wherever it appears

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[NARRATIVE]
UID: NAR-CANON-COLOURS
TITLE: What a colour means, wherever it appears
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: table
PLACE: card
TAGS: colours
STATEMENT: >>>
| colour | means |
| green | it holds as written, or it is in force |
| teal | designed or recorded, but not built and not proven |
| blue | an open question, and somebody has to answer it |
| amber | incomplete or low confidence: it wants attention and is not broken |
| red | missing: it is needed and nobody owns it |
| slate | nothing owed here: dissolved, already covered elsewhere, or unchanged |
| violet | reserved; no system uses it yet |
| grey | a marker, not a verdict |
<<<
